    "problem_statement": "The event API lacks a wait variant that atomically clears the events it returns. A consumer that waits for a set of events, receives them, and then waits again for the same events is given those same events a second time (\"phantom events\"), because the events remain in the event object after being delivered. The capability required is a wait that, on match, removes the matched events from the event object so that a subsequent wait for the same events returns nothing until the events are set/posted again \u2014 for both \"wait for any\" and \"wait for all\" semantics.",
